# Agent tooling — these MUST live here, NOT in .git/info/exclude.
#
# .claude/ was ignored only via .git/info/exclude, which is LOCAL and UNVERSIONED: it does not
# survive a `git clone`, so on any other machine .claude/ (agent worktrees, several GB) is unignored
# and stageable. That is the same class of bug as .serena/ (internal work item 412) — a protection that looks in place
# and evaporates on clone.
#
# It matters because an MCP server's TOOL surface does not bound its WRITE surface: Serena's
# file-writing tools are disabled in this context and its language server still wrote 235 metadata
# files into the source tree. A stray `git add -A` is all it takes to commit someone else's writes.
#
# EXCEPTION 1: `.claude/settings.json` is the COMMITTED, portable team declaration (P-046 T06 internal work item 438) —
# marketplaces + plugin allowlist + telemetry-off. Everything else under .claude/ stays ignored
# (worktrees, .cc-writes, and the machine-local settings.local.json). Uses `.claude/*` + a re-include,
# not `.claude/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded outright.
#
# EXCEPTION 2: `.claude/skills/` is where an agent discovers REPO-WIDE skills, so a skill that is not
# re-included here is a skill nobody but its author can invoke (N06 S07, internal work item 731). It holds a SYMLINK,
# `add-appbase-service` -> `appbase-codeagents/claude/skills/add-appbase-service`, so the recipes stay
# where their history is and the discovery path stays one line.
#
# ⚠️ THE RE-INCLUDE IS PER-ENTRY, AND IT HAS TO BE. `!.claude/skills` alone un-ignores the WHOLE
# SUBTREE at unlimited depth — `.claude/*` is single-segment, so `*` never crosses `/` and nothing
# re-ignores the descendants. That is functionally identical to `!.claude/skills/**`, and it would hand
# a stray `git add -A` everything that ever lands under `.claude/skills/` — which is exactly where
# skill-authoring and plugin tooling writes. The paragraph above is about an MCP server putting 235
# files into the tree with no tool call and no prompt; this is that same door, one level down.
#
# So: re-include the directory, RE-EXCLUDE its contents, then re-include the one entry by name. Adding
# a second skill means adding a second `!` line — deliberately, so each one is a decision somebody made.
#
# ⚠️ Verified by execution in BOTH directions, because a rule like this cannot be read for correctness:
#   discovery  — `claude -p` listing skills returns `add-appbase-service`; `NONE` with the symlink moved away
#   breadth    — `.claude/skills/<probe>/evil.md` is IGNORED; `add-appbase-service` is NOT
#   neighbours — `settings.local.json`, `worktrees/`, `.cc-writes/` all still ignored
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/add-appbase-service
# The second `!` line the paragraph above asks for, and a decision somebody made: `appbase-code-review`
# is the MANDATORY pre-PR gate (internal work item 833). Left un-re-included it would be discoverable only on the machine
# that authored it — and the whole point of vendoring it was that the plugin's version was unreachable
# to the agent and unrunnable in the container.
!.claude/skills/appbase-code-review
# The THIRD `!` line, same reasoning, and the reason is now measured rather than argued:
# `appbase-security-review` (internal work item 733) replaces a harness gate that read the WRONG TREE four times --
# ~400 files against a 10-file change -- and was aborted by hand every time. Left un-re-included it
# would exist only on the machine that authored it, which for a MANDATORY gate is the same as not
# existing. `scripts/test/claude_skills_test.sh` asserts every mandated skill is tracked, not merely
# present, because a working-tree check passes happily over a file git will never ship.
!.claude/skills/appbase-security-review

