# ── MCP-server write paths (internal work item 420 / N14, second pass) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# All four installed MCP servers run with CWD = the REPO ROOT — verified with `lsof -a -p <pid> -d cwd`
# on the live processes. Every relative-path write they make therefore lands in the source tree.
#
# These are ignored so they can never be COMMITTED, and listed in .tripwire-watch so that ignoring
# them does not also make them INVISIBLE — `git status --porcelain` omits ignored entries, so before
# the watch list a path was covered by one mechanism or the other and never both.
#
# firebase (`firebase experimental:mcp`): firebase_init/deploy write these into CWD; lib/utils.js
# also builds its debug-log path as `path.join(process.cwd(), "firebase-debug.log")`.
/.firebase/
/.firebaserc
/firebase.json
# dart (`dart mcp-server`, 24 features all enabled): its root IS the repo root, so an analyzer or
# `pub` invocation there lands at top level. Module-level .gitignore files do not cover the root.
/.dart_tool/
# Generated by the dart MCP's `pub` tool, never hand-edited. Previously TRACKED and unignored, so a
# regeneration appeared as ` M` — indistinguishable from a deliberate edit. That is the CHANGELOG.adoc
# sweep (internal work item 413) with a live writer attached. The sibling module already ignored its copies; the
# inconsistency was the bug.
# ⚠️ Ignoring these DOES reduce their visibility to zero, and that is accepted knowingly, not
# overlooked: they are supposed to exist, so .tripwire-watch (whose criterion is "nothing should be
# creating this") is the wrong instrument — see the note there. Change-detection for files that
# legitimately exist is internal work item 581.

# Generated Playwright HTML report (regenerated per run; not tracked)
appbase-config-wizard/test/web/playwright-report/
